    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>A single city-state created in 408 BCE by the union of the three old cities of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#rhodes">Rhodes</a>: Ialysos, Kamiros and Lindos.</li><li>Its skilled navy policed the eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#mediterranean">Mediterranean</a> and protected the grain trade, making it the leading Hellenistic sea power.</li><li><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#rome">Rome</a>’s punishment in 167 BCE broke its economy, and it lost its freedom to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#claudius">Claudius</a> and finally to Vespasian.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#colossus-of-rhodes">Colossus</a> fell in an earthquake, its remains lay where they had fallen for centuries; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#pliny-the-elder">Pliny the Elder</a> wrote that few people could wrap their arms around its thumb.</p></aside>
    </section>

